            </profile>
            <profile id="7385-5298-57a5-222c" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="15ea-5299-d0f5-5dbb" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Hand weapon, shield, light armour and either Kontarion or Heavy Maces. May ride warhorses (+3 pts), have heavy armour (+1 pt) and half-barding (+2 pts) or barding (+4 pts). Superior Byzantine Cavalry. Combined Formation - every other model may exchange Kontarion or Heavy Mace for bow, but may take no more equipment if they do so - archers are placed in the rear ranks. The Emperor's Guards must be the smallest cavalry unit in the army, and must be led by the Emperor at all times. Komnenian armies: the Emperor's Guards may exchange Kontarion for lance (+2 pts). 0-1 units. (Byzantium p.95)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
