  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="c867-585a-8339-6315" name="Late Byzantines (Byzantium) - List Notes" publicationId="15ea-5299-d0f5-5dbb" hidden="false">
      <description>LATE BYZANTINES (Byzantium: Beyond the Golden Gate, pp.90-95): the Macedonian Successors and the Komnenian Dynasty, 1042-1185 AD. From the middle of the 11th Century the Theme system was largely replaced by wholly professional regiments and mercenaries.

ARMY COMPOSITIONS (pick one in the Army composition list):
[Late Byzantines - Macedonian Successors]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Infantry: up to 75%
  Cavalry: at least 25%
  Special Units: up to 25%
  Allies and Mercenaries: up to 33%
  MACEDONIAN SUCCESSORS (1042-1081 AD). Characters up to 25%; Infantry up to 75%; Cavalry at least 25% (two units of Skythikoi may be chosen); Special Units up to 25%; Allies &amp; Mercenaries up to 33% on Pechenegs and Alans (Steppe Nomads list; documented only) - none of the troops listed as Allies &amp; Mercenaries here may be chosen. Special rules: one unit of Light Pronoiarios may be upgraded to Prokousatores (+1 pt per model; no more than 25% bows; Feigned Flight). Up to two characters may be drawn from the Thematic Byzantines list (only Themata Commanders, including a Strategos, who may not be Army General - documented only). The Englino-Varangoi Guards may be Fearsome (+2 pts).
[Late Byzantines - Komnenian Dynasty]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Infantry: up to 50%
  Cavalry: up to 75%
  Special Units: up to 33%
  Allies and Mercenaries: up to 33%
  KOMNENIAN DYNASTY (1081-1185 AD). Characters up to 25%; Infantry up to 50%; Cavalry up to 75% (for every unit of Kavallarioi Guards, a unit of Regular or Irregular Kavallarioi must be taken as well - not enforced); Special Units up to 33%; Allies &amp; Mercenaries up to 33% on the Allied &amp; Mercenary troops below, and on Pechenegs, Cumans and Alans (Steppe Nomads list - documented only); Allies may also be drawn from Westerners from the early Crusades and from Crusader States (use the AoA Crusader list - documented only). Special rules: Guard Kavallarioi and the Emperor's Guards may exchange Kontarion for lance (+2 pts); such units imitate western knights - they cannot combine with archers, and no longer count as Superior Byzantine Cavalry; they may count their rank bonus up to +1. Latinikoi Cavalry may ride barded warhorses (+4 pts). Instead of taking Solenarion, one unit of Regular Psiloi may exchange javelins or sling for a crossbow (+4 pts).</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
